,-88.5,1014.5],[-22.8,-82.8,1015.9],[-17.1,-77.1,1017.6],[-11.5,-71.5,1019.7],[-5.8,-65.8,1022.2],[-0.2,-60.2,1024.8],[5.5,-54.5,1027.5],[11.1,-48.9,1029.7],[16.3,-42.8,1032.0],[20.4,-36.0,1034.8],[22.4,-28.2,1037.9],[22.1,-20.4,1041.1],[20.5,-12.6,1044.4],[16.2,-6.2,1047.1]],"mapped_n":1,"km":0.19,"mapped_km":0.0,"traced_km":0.19,"climb_m":43},"buildings":[],"streams":[{"kind":"river","name":null,"pts":[[1488.6,1274.8],[1487.0,1265.0],[1485.3,1255.1],[1483.7,1245.3],[1482.0,1235.4],[1480.4,1225.5],[1478.8,1215.7],[1477.1,1205.8],[1477.4,1196.0],[1479.6,1186.2],[1481.7,1176.4],[1483.9,1166.7],[1486.0,1156.9],[1486.6,1154.0]]}],"facts":{"drive_km":0.6,"drive_start_m":916,"drive_end_m":995,"drive_climb_m":79,"drive_max_grade_pct":20,"drive_minutes_at_9kmh":4,"walk_km":0.19,"walk_mapped_km":0.0,"walk_traced_km":0.19,"walk_climb_m":43,"box_km":[3.01,2.99],"arrival_m":1053},"edits":["A bench up to 24 m wide is cut along the jeep track to the smoothed track profile (the 30 m DSM includes tree canopy).","Road bumps and ruts in the drive are illustrative; the grade and the line of the track are real.","Trees, shrubs, grass tufts and boulders are placed where WorldCover maps that cover; their size and number are illustrative.","The walking loop is a 150 m circle around the arrival point; it is not a mapped trail.","Trees within 45 m of the Mahmud Ghaznavi Mosque are left out so it can be seen; WorldCover 2021 maps tree cover there.","The mosque is drawn from the plan in the Wikipedia article: a rectangular prayer hall 28 m by 21 m, the mihrab square and centred in the west wall, an off-centre entrance in the east wall, a paved courtyard with a sunken ablution tank in the middle, three oblong rooms (ziyada) to the north and three bastions on their outer side. Front faces the qibla (254 degrees, computed from the coordinates).","Estimated, not published: the pillar base positions (5 by 8 as the article gives them), the tank size, the wall thickness and height (about 1.5 m, from the photos; the article mentions traces of 30-foot walls, which are not drawn at full height), the mihrab projection, the stone stair on the east side and the boulders.","The levelled ground is a 22 m radius terrace; the platform is 34 m by 27 m (estimated) and its straight stone retaining walls sit on the downhill sides (the article says the mosque stands on an early artificial terrace); the slope beyond it is the DEM.","The OSM archaeological-site outline (about 73 m by 33 m) is not drawn as a footprint; the walking circle is a 36 m circle around the point, not a mapped path.","Trees within 45 m of the mosque are left out so it can be seen; WorldCover 2021 maps tree cover there.","The walk from the end of the jeep track follows the mapped OSM footpath for 0.0 km; the last 0.19 km is not mapped and is traced over the ground (easiest slope on the DEM).","Season colours, snow, ice and dawn mist are illustrative.","Traffic on the drive is illustrative: the vehicle kinds are those seen on Swat roads (Willys jeeps, Hilux, Suzuki vans, Mehran cars, CD70 motorbikes, Qingqi rickshaws, painted trucks); their number and movement are not counted."],"sources":[{"name":"Copernicus DEM GLO-30","use":"terrain heights","licence":"© DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018, provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA","url":"https://spacedata.copernicus.eu/collections/copernicus-digital-elevation-model"},{"name":"ESA WorldCover 10 m 2021 v200","use":"trees, meadow, rock, snow","licence":"CC BY 4.0, © ESA WorldCover project 2021","url":"https://esa-worldcover.org"},{"name":"Wikipedia: Mahmud Ghaznavi Mosque","use":"plan (28 m by 21 m), pillar bases, mihrab and entrance positions, courtyard and tank, ziyada rooms and bastions, dates and quotes","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahmud_Ghaznavi_Mosque"},{"name":"OpenStreetMap","use":"the OSM road to Odigram (its end is the trailhead, about 170 m from the mosque), the archaeological-site outline and the buildings near the site","licence":"ODbL, © OpenStreetMap contributors","url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright"}]}